  "diagnosis": {
    "answer_markdown": "- The latest projected Pod phase is Pending.\n- The latest projected PodScheduled condition is True.\n- An older FailedScheduling Event was also observed.\n- The Pod has a projected ReplicaSet owner relationship.\n\nA previous scheduling block may have cleared, leaving a different Pending-stage issue. Confidence: high. To verify: A fresh bounded observation again reports PodScheduled=False with a current FailedScheduling Event.\n\nThe FailedScheduling Event predates the latest scheduled condition. Impact: It cannot establish the current reason for the Pending phase.\n\nThe older FailedScheduling Event and current PodScheduled=True condition describe different states. Impact: A definite current scheduling root cause would overstate the observations.\n\nSuggested next step: Collect a fresh bounded Pod and Event observation before changing scheduling configuration. Risk: Acting on stale scheduling information may address the wrong stage. Before acting: Keep the same active ClusterScope for the new observation.",
